What I do when I have a certain item that I really want to know to be 
cursed or not is the following (still not fool proof):

  +--------+
  |.f..C...|
  |....?.@.-
  |....C...|
  +--------+

I put the item I want to BUC-ID on the ?-spot, and two confirmed cursed 
items on the C-spots. Now, I wait. My pet will normally tend to move in 
my direction. However, if the ?-item is cursed, it will stay on the 
other side of the C?C-line. If the ?-item is not cursed, it will easily 
cross the C?C-line and thus approach me.

This will also work in corridors, of course. Drop the item somewhere in 
a corridor, and leave your pet on the other side. The longer it takes 
for her to approach you, the more certain you can be that the item's 
cursed. For this to work you will have to stand somewhere you're able to 
see the item, of course, so you'll get the "reluctantly" message.

